IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g7-fourth-schedule`

-- g7-commencement.l4: section 63 of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or Air-Conditioning
-- Systems Law 5785-2025: commencement and application.
--
-- Written by ENCODER G7.  Imports `prelude`, `daydate`, the vendored `il-interpretation-time`, `domain`, and the
-- sibling module `g7-fourth-schedule` of this group (same prefix, no cross-group import).
--
-- What section 63 says, and how it is encoded.
--   (a) The Law, except Chapter 6, commences as regards the performance of work on a system, in two regimes by refrigerant:
--       (1) a system that operates by means of a flammable refrigerant listed in the Fourth Schedule, provided its
--           use is permitted by any law: three months from the Law's publication, or the entry into force of the
--           regulations under section 59, whichever is later.  That date is "the commencement day".
--       (2) a system that operates by means of a refrigerant not as stated in (1): 18 months from the commencement day.
--       The Minister, after consulting the Minister of Environmental Protection, may amend the Fourth Schedule by order.
--   (b) Chapter 6: 18 months from the commencement day, or the entry into force of regulations under section 46,
--       whichever is later.
--
-- The facts are inputs and are never collapsed into one date (the fleet lead's ruling 3): the day of the Law's
-- publication, the day the section 59 regulations came into force (decided by G8), and a MAYBE date for regulations
-- under section 46 (none are in the sources).  The consumers' booleans of PLAN IP2 and IP16 are computed here.
--
-- Time is counted only through the vendored module `il-interpretation-time`: no `add months`, no `add years`, and no
-- PLUS on a date.  The later of two days is a comparison.
--   * "N months from a day" is the Interpretation Law s.10(b): it ends on the same-numbered day of the month N
--     later, or the month's last day.  The Law commences ON that day.  (Fork F-C-4: the day after.)
--   * The fleet lead's ruling 4 applies IL s.10(c) to a deadline (D) and to a window (W) and does NOT apply it to a
--     period of validity (V) or to a commencement counted from another date (C).  Every period here is kind C.
--     (Fork F-C-1: the alternative is a callable reading.)
-- Kind X, a length fixed by an official, is in g7-regulations.l4 (section 60(2)(a)).  No period of kind D, V or W
-- is met in sections 58 to 63.  Periods counted backwards are not met either.
--
-- The classification of a system by its refrigerants (paragraphs (1) and (2)) matters only between the commencement
-- day and the day paragraph (2) takes effect: before the first no regime has commenced, from the second both have.
-- The rules answer outside that window without classifying, so a system with no recorded refrigerant, or one the text
-- does not classify, is a named REFUSE only when the answer depends on it.
--
-- The Fourth Schedule is the Schedule as enacted.  An order under section 63(a)(1) would be a new vintage of the
-- list, which this fleet does not model (ruling 2); the Minister's power to make one is encoded below.

§ `63. Commencement and application`

§§ `The facts that fix the commencement`

-- Inputs under their standard names (PLAN section (c)): IP13 `the s.59 regulations came into force on` (decided
-- by G8: regulation 5 of the Fees Regulations, 7 days from 9.7.2025, so 16.7.2025).
@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462); s.63(a)(2) (src:463); s.63(b) (src:464)
@desc The facts that section 63 counts from: the Law's publication, the entry into force of the regulations under section 59, and the entry into force of any regulations under section 46
DECLARE `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63` HAS
    `the day the Law was published in Reshumot` IS A DATE @desc The day the Law was published in Reshumot (Sefer HaChukim 3349): 14.1.2025 by the gazette. Not the day the Knesset passed it (8.1.2025)
    `the s.59 regulations came into force on` IS A DATE @desc The day the regulations under section 59 (the Fees Regulations) came into force: 16.7.2025 by regulation 5 of the Fees Regulations, decided by the Fees group
    `the day regulations under section 46 came into force, if any` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The day regulations under section 46 came into force; NOTHING if none are known to be in force (none appear in the sources)

-- The three open choices about how the dates are counted.  The record of the readings taken is `the readings of
-- the dates taken`; each alternative is a record built below, and every date function takes the record, so each
-- alternative is a call of the same function.
@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462); s.63(a)(2) (src:463); s.63(b) (src:464)
@desc The choices the text of section 63 leaves open for counting its dates; the reading taken is the record named `the readings of the dates taken`
DECLARE `Readings of the dates of section 63` HAS
    `IL s.10(c) is applied to a period counted from another date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True to apply the Interpretation Law's section 10(c) (a period does not end on a day of rest, recess or holiday) to the periods of months counted from another date; the reading taken is FALSE
    `the Law commences on the day after a period of months ends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True to read a commencement "N months from" a day as the day AFTER the last day of the period; the reading taken is FALSE, the Law commencing on the last day of the period itself
    `the three months of paragraph (1) run from the later of the two days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True to read "three months from its publication or the entry into force of the regulations, whichever is later" as three months counted from the later of those two days; the reading taken is FALSE, the later of the end of three months from publication and the entry into force
    `the calendar of rest days` IS A `Calendar of rest days` @desc The days of rest, recess or holiday, used only when section 10(c) of the Interpretation Law is applied; never computed

@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462); s.63(a)(2) (src:463); s.63(b) (src:464)
GIVETH A `Readings of the dates of section 63`
`the readings of the dates taken` MEANS
    `Readings of the dates of section 63` WITH
        `IL s.10(c) is applied to a period counted from another date` IS FALSE
        `the Law commences on the day after a period of months ends` IS FALSE
        `the three months of paragraph (1) run from the later of the two days` IS FALSE
        `the calendar of rest days` IS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS EMPTY

§§ `Counting a period of months from another date (kind C)`

-- The one place a period of months is counted.  The end is the Interpretation Law s.10(b) (the same-numbered day
-- of the month N later, or the month's last day, and that day is inside the period).  Under the reading taken
-- the Law commences on that day.  Each alternative reading changes one thing: the end is first moved by IL s.10(c)
-- (fork F-C-1), or the Law commences on the day after the period ends (fork F-C-4).
-- The days of rest are an input and are never computed.
@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462); s.63(a)(2) (src:463); s.63(b) (src:464)
GIVEN months IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
      readings IS A `Readings of the dates of section 63`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 63 — the day the Law commences, N months from the day` months d `, under the readings` readings MEANS
    IF   readings's `the Law commences on the day after a period of months ends`
    THEN `s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 1 `days from` end
    ELSE end
    WHERE
        end MEANS
            IF   readings's `IL s.10(c) is applied to a period counted from another date`
            THEN `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` months `months after an event on` d
                     `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are`
                     (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` ((readings's `the calendar of rest days`)'s `days of rest, recess or holiday`))
            ELSE `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` months `months after an event on` d

-- The later of two days; section 63 says "whichever is later" twice.
@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462); s.63(b) (src:464)
GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 63 — the later of` a `and` b MEANS
    IF   a AT LEAST b
    THEN a
    ELSE b

§§ `63(a)(1). The commencement day`

-- src:461 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} לעניין ביצוע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר הפועלת באמצעות קרר דליק המנוי {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 4|בתוספת הרביעית}}, ובלבד שהשימוש בו הותר על פי כל דין – שלושה חודשים מיום פרסומו או מועד כניסתן לתוקף של תקנות לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 59|סעיף 59}}, לפי המאוחר (להלן – יום התחילה); השר, לאחר התייעצות עם השר להגנת הסביבה, רשאי לשנות, בצו, את {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 4|התוספת הרביעית}};
-- src:462 | {{ח:תתת}} {{ח:הערה|(תחילתן של התקנות לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 59|סעיף 59}}, היא ביום 16.7.2025).}}
@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
      readings IS A `Readings of the dates of section 63`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 63(a)(1) — the commencement day, under the readings` facts readings MEANS
    IF   readings's `the three months of paragraph (1) run from the later of the two days`
    THEN `s 63 — the day the Law commences, N months from the day` 3
             (`s 63 — the later of` (facts's `the day the Law was published in Reshumot`) `and` (facts's `the s.59 regulations came into force on`))
             `, under the readings` readings
    ELSE `s 63 — the later of`
             (`s 63 — the day the Law commences, N months from the day` 3 (facts's `the day the Law was published in Reshumot`) `, under the readings` readings)
             `and`
             (facts's `the s.59 regulations came into force on`)

@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462)
@export The commencement day of the Israeli Law on work on refrigeration and air-conditioning systems (section 63(a)(1)): the later of three months from the Law's publication and the entry into force of the regulations under section 59
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63` @desc The Law's publication day, the day the section 59 regulations came into force, and the day any section 46 regulations came into force
GIVETH A DATE
`the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` facts MEANS
    `s 63(a)(1) — the commencement day, under the readings` facts `the readings of the dates taken`

§§ `63(a)(2). The Law for a system with any other refrigerant`

-- src:463 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} לעניין ביצוע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר הפועלת באמצעות קרר שאינו כאמור בפסקה (1) – 18 חודשים מיום התחילה.
@ref s.63(a)(2) (src:463)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
      readings IS A `Readings of the dates of section 63`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 63(a)(2) — the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant, under the readings` facts readings MEANS
    `s 63 — the day the Law commences, N months from the day` 18
        (`s 63(a)(1) — the commencement day, under the readings` facts readings)
        `, under the readings` readings

@ref s.63(a)(2) (src:463)
@export The day the Israeli Law on work on refrigeration and air-conditioning systems commences for a system that operates by means of a refrigerant other than a lawful listed flammable one (section 63(a)(2)): 18 months from the commencement day
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63` @desc The Law's publication day, the day the section 59 regulations came into force, and the day any section 46 regulations came into force
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant under section 63(a)(2)` facts MEANS
    `s 63(a)(2) — the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant, under the readings` facts `the readings of the dates taken`

§§ `63(a)(1), (2). Which paragraph governs a system: its refrigerants`

-- The two regimes.  A system is placed by its refrigerants, listed in the Fourth Schedule and lawful for (1), any
-- other for (2).  The words leave three questions open, each a fork in FRAGMENT-G7.md and each a reading below:
--   F-C-6a  a system with SEVERAL refrigerants, some as stated in (1) and some not: both paragraphs' words are met;
--   F-C-6b  a listed refrigerant whose use is NOT permitted by law: (1) requires lawful use, (2) is "not as stated in (1)";
--   F-C-6c  a system with NO refrigerant recorded: the text says nothing.
@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462); s.63(a)(2) (src:463)
@desc The two commencement regimes of section 63(a): paragraph (1) for a lawful listed flammable refrigerant, paragraph (2) for any other
DECLARE `Commencement regime of section 63(a)` IS ONE OF
    `the regime of paragraph (1)`   -- a flammable refrigerant listed in the Fourth Schedule whose use is permitted by law
    `the regime of paragraph (2)`   -- a refrigerant that is not as stated in paragraph (1)

@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462)
@desc How a system with several refrigerants is classified when some are as stated in paragraph (1) and some are not
DECLARE `Reading of a system with several refrigerants` IS ONE OF
    `paragraph (1) governs a system if any of its refrigerants is as stated in it`           -- the reading taken: the Law applies from the earliest date either paragraph gives
    `paragraph (1) governs a system only if every one of its refrigerants is as stated in it` -- the later date governs a mixed system
    `the text is taken not to say which paragraph governs a system with refrigerants of both kinds`

@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462)
@desc How a refrigerant that is listed in the Fourth Schedule but whose use is not permitted by law is classified
DECLARE `Reading of a listed refrigerant whose use is not permitted` IS ONE OF
    `such a refrigerant is not as stated in paragraph (1), so paragraph (2) governs`   -- the reading taken: (2) is the complement of (1)
    `the text is taken not to say which paragraph governs such a refrigerant`

@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462); s.63(a)(2) (src:463)
@desc The two choices the text of section 63(a) leaves open for classifying a system by its refrigerants
DECLARE `Readings of the regime of section 63(a)` HAS
    `how a system with several refrigerants is classified` IS A `Reading of a system with several refrigerants` @desc The reading taken is that paragraph (1) governs if any refrigerant is as stated in it
    `how a listed refrigerant whose use is not permitted is classified` IS A `Reading of a listed refrigerant whose use is not permitted` @desc The reading taken is that such a refrigerant is not as stated in paragraph (1), so paragraph (2) governs

@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462); s.63(a)(2) (src:463)
GIVETH A `Readings of the regime of section 63(a)`
`the readings of the regime taken` MEANS
    `Readings of the regime of section 63(a)` WITH
        `how a system with several refrigerants is classified` IS `paragraph (1) governs a system if any of its refrigerants is as stated in it`
        `how a listed refrigerant whose use is not permitted is classified` IS `such a refrigerant is not as stated in paragraph (1), so paragraph (2) governs`

-- Named refusals, each returned in the position of an answer and never stored.
@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462); s.63(a)(2) (src:463)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`no refrigerant is recorded for the system, and section 63(a) classifies a system by its refrigerant` MEANS
    REFUSE "no refrigerant is recorded for the system, and section 63(a) classifies a system by its refrigerant"

@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462); s.63(a)(2) (src:463)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text of section 63(a)(1) and (2) does not say which paragraph governs a listed refrigerant whose use is not permitted by law` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text of section 63(a)(1) and (2) does not say which paragraph governs a listed refrigerant whose use is not permitted by law"

@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462); s.63(a)(2) (src:463)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text of section 63(a)(1) and (2) does not say which paragraph governs a system with refrigerants of both kinds` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text of section 63(a)(1) and (2) does not say which paragraph governs a system with refrigerants of both kinds"

-- The proviso of (1) is said of the refrigerant ("whose use was permitted by any law"): listed and lawful.
@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461)
GIVEN r IS A Refrigerant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63(a)(1) — the refrigerant is a listed flammable refrigerant whose use is permitted by law` r MEANS
        `a refrigerant is a listed flammable refrigerant` r
    AND r's `use of the refrigerant is permitted by law`

@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461); s.63(a)(2) (src:463)
GIVEN r IS A Refrigerant
      readings IS A `Readings of the regime of section 63(a)`
GIVETH A `Commencement regime of section 63(a)`
`s 63(a) — the regime of the refrigerant, under the readings` r readings MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   `s 63(a)(1) — the refrigerant is a listed flammable refrigerant whose use is permitted by law` r
        THEN `the regime of paragraph (1)`
        IF   `a refrigerant is a listed flammable refrigerant` r
             AND readings's `how a listed refrigerant whose use is not permitted is classified`
                 EQUALS `the text is taken not to say which paragraph governs such a refrigerant`
        THEN `the text of section 63(a)(1) and (2) does not say which paragraph governs a listed refrigerant whose use is not permitted by law`
        OTHERWISE `the regime of paragraph (2)`

@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462); s.63(a)(2) (src:463)
GIVEN system IS A `Cooling system`
      readings IS A `Readings of the regime of section 63(a)`
GIVETH A `Commencement regime of section 63(a)`
`s 63(a) — the regime of the system, under the readings` system readings MEANS
    IF   null (system's `refrigerants`)
    THEN `no refrigerant is recorded for the system, and section 63(a) classifies a system by its refrigerant`
    ELSE CONSIDER readings's `how a system with several refrigerants is classified`
         WHEN `paragraph (1) governs a system if any of its refrigerants is as stated in it`
         THEN IF   any `in paragraph (1)` (system's `refrigerants`)
              THEN `the regime of paragraph (1)`
              ELSE `the regime of paragraph (2)`
         WHEN `paragraph (1) governs a system only if every one of its refrigerants is as stated in it`
         THEN IF   all `in paragraph (1)` (system's `refrigerants`)
              THEN `the regime of paragraph (1)`
              ELSE `the regime of paragraph (2)`
         WHEN `the text is taken not to say which paragraph governs a system with refrigerants of both kinds`
         THEN IF   all `in paragraph (1)` (system's `refrigerants`)
              THEN `the regime of paragraph (1)`
              ELSE IF   all `in paragraph (2)` (system's `refrigerants`)
                   THEN `the regime of paragraph (2)`
                   ELSE `the text of section 63(a)(1) and (2) does not say which paragraph governs a system with refrigerants of both kinds`
    WHERE
        `in paragraph (1)` r MEANS
            `s 63(a) — the regime of the refrigerant, under the readings` r readings EQUALS `the regime of paragraph (1)`
        `in paragraph (2)` r MEANS
            `s 63(a) — the regime of the refrigerant, under the readings` r readings EQUALS `the regime of paragraph (2)`

@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462); s.63(a)(2) (src:463)
GIVEN system IS A `Cooling system` @desc The system: its cooling capacity and the refrigerants it operates by, each with its designation and whether its use is permitted by law
GIVETH A `Commencement regime of section 63(a)`
`the regime of a system under section 63(a)` system MEANS
    `s 63(a) — the regime of the system, under the readings` system `the readings of the regime taken`

§§ `63(a). Whether the Law has commenced for work on a system on a day`

-- The consumers' boolean of PLAN IP2, "the Law has commenced for the work on the system".  The question is asked of
-- a DAY: a day on or after the commencement of the regime that governs the system.  Whether the commencement day
-- binds from the first minute of the day or from 00.01 (Interpretation Law s.21) is a fork (F-C-5): the moment-level
-- function below is the alternative.
-- src:460 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} תחילתו של חוק זה, למעט {{ח:פנימי|פרק ו|פרק ו׳}} –
-- src:461 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} לעניין ביצוע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר הפועלת באמצעות קרר דליק המנוי {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 4|בתוספת הרביעית}}, ובלבד שהשימוש בו הותר על פי כל דין – שלושה חודשים מיום פרסומו או מועד כניסתן לתוקף של תקנות לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 59|סעיף 59}}, לפי המאוחר (להלן – יום התחילה); השר, לאחר התייעצות עם השר להגנת הסביבה, רשאי לשנות, בצו, את {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 4|התוספת הרביעית}};
-- src:462 | {{ח:תתת}} {{ח:הערה|(תחילתן של התקנות לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 59|סעיף 59}}, היא ביום 16.7.2025).}}
-- src:463 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} לעניין ביצוע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר הפועלת באמצעות קרר שאינו כאמור בפסקה (1) – 18 חודשים מיום התחילה.
@ref s.63(a) (src:460-463)
GIVEN system IS A `Cooling system`
      day IS A DATE
      facts IS A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
      dateReadings IS A `Readings of the dates of section 63`
      regimeReadings IS A `Readings of the regime of section 63(a)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` system day facts dateReadings regimeReadings MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   day LESS THAN (`s 63(a)(1) — the commencement day, under the readings` facts dateReadings)
        THEN FALSE
        IF   day AT LEAST (`s 63(a)(2) — the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant, under the readings` facts dateReadings)
        THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `s 63(a) — the regime of the system, under the readings` system regimeReadings
            WHEN `the regime of paragraph (1)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the regime of paragraph (2)` THEN FALSE

@ref s.63(a) (src:460-463)
@export Whether the Israeli Law on work on refrigeration and air-conditioning systems has commenced, on the given day, for work on a cooling system, by section 63(a): a lawful listed flammable refrigerant from the commencement day, any other refrigerant 18 months later
GIVEN system IS A `Cooling system` @desc The system: its cooling capacity and the refrigerants it operates by, each with its designation (for example 290 or 134a, no leading R) and whether its use is permitted by law
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about, for example the day the work was done
      facts IS A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63` @desc The Law's publication day, the day the section 59 regulations came into force, and the day any section 46 regulations came into force
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Law has commenced for work on the system` system `on the day` day `given the facts` facts MEANS
    `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` system day facts `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime taken`

@ref s.63(a) (src:460-463)
GIVEN item IS A `Work item`
      facts IS A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Law has commenced for the work item` item `given the facts` facts MEANS
    `the Law has commenced for work on the system` (item's `the system`) `on the day` (item's `date performed`) `given the facts` facts

-- The same question at a MOMENT, by the Interpretation Law s.21: the Law binds from 00:01 on the commencement day.
-- Before the commencement day's 00:01, no regime binds; from the day paragraph (2) takes effect, both do.
@ref s.63(a) (src:460-463)
GIVEN system IS A `Cooling system`
      moment IS A Moment
      facts IS A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
      dateReadings IS A `Readings of the dates of section 63`
      regimeReadings IS A `Readings of the regime of section 63(a)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63(a) and IL s.21 — under the readings, the Law binds work on the system at the moment` system moment facts dateReadings regimeReadings MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   NOT `s 21 — the moment` moment `is one at which a statute commencing on`
                    (`s 63(a)(1) — the commencement day, under the readings` facts dateReadings) `binds`
        THEN FALSE
        IF   `s 21 — the moment` moment `is one at which a statute commencing on`
                    (`s 63(a)(2) — the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant, under the readings` facts dateReadings) `binds`
        THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `s 63(a) — the regime of the system, under the readings` system regimeReadings
            WHEN `the regime of paragraph (1)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the regime of paragraph (2)` THEN FALSE

§§ `63(a). The provisions that are not about work on a system (trap T20)`

-- Section 63(a) fixes a commencement only "for the performance of work on a system".  It says nothing about the
-- Registrar, the Council, inspection, applications or the Minister's powers, and the sources give no default
-- commencement day for a law that fixes none (the Interpretation NOTES, fork F26).  The encoding does not pick one.
@ref s.63(a) (src:460-463)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 63(a) fixes a commencement only for the performance of work on a system, and gives no day for the other provisions of the Law` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 63(a) fixes a commencement only for the performance of work on a system, and gives no day for the other provisions of the Law"

@ref s.63(a) (src:460-463)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Law has commenced, for a provision that is not about work on a system, on the day` day MEANS
    `section 63(a) fixes a commencement only for the performance of work on a system, and gives no day for the other provisions of the Law`

§§ `63(a)(1), last clause. The Minister's power to amend the Fourth Schedule`

-- The Minister, after consulting the Minister of Environmental Protection, may amend the Fourth Schedule by
-- order.  The content of an order is an input and is not in the sources: the Schedule as enacted is the only
-- vintage modelled (ruling 2).  The power carries no deadline.
@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461)
@desc What the Minister does to the Fourth Schedule
DECLARE `Act of the Minister on the Fourth Schedule` IS ONE OF
    `amend the Fourth Schedule by order`

@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461)
GIVEN `the Minister consulted the Minister of Environmental Protection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Minister of Labour consulted the Minister of Environmental Protection before making the order
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63(a)(1) — the consultation needed for an order amending the Fourth Schedule has taken place` `the Minister consulted the Minister of Environmental Protection` MEANS
    `the Minister consulted the Minister of Environmental Protection`

@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461)
GIVEN `the Minister consulted the Minister of Environmental Protection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act of the Minister on the Fourth Schedule`
`s 63(a)(1) — the Minister's power to amend the Fourth Schedule by order` `the Minister consulted the Minister of Environmental Protection` MEANS
    IF   `s 63(a)(1) — the consultation needed for an order amending the Fourth Schedule has taken place` `the Minister consulted the Minister of Environmental Protection`
    THEN PARTY `the Minister` MAY `amend the Fourth Schedule by order`
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `63(b). Chapter 6`

-- Chapter 6 (the financial sanctions) commences 18 months from the commencement day, or on the entry into force
-- of regulations under section 46, whichever is later.  Section 46(b) is a power ("may") to make those
-- regulations (trap T19): if none is ever made, the later date does not exist and the text gives Chapter 6 no
-- commencement.  `NOTHING` therefore means "no regulation under section 46 is known", and the answer that depends on
-- it is a named REFUSE; the closed-world reading, that no regulation means "not yet", is a fork (F-C-8).
@ref s.63(b) (src:464)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 63(b) starts Chapter 6 at the later of 18 months from the commencement day and the entry into force of regulations under section 46, and none are in the sources` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 63(b) starts Chapter 6 at the later of 18 months from the commencement day and the entry into force of regulations under section 46, and none are in the sources"

-- src:464 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} תחילתו של {{ח:פנימי|פרק ו|פרק ו׳}} 18 חודשים מיום התחילה או במועד כניסתן לתוקף של תקנות לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 46|סעיף 46}}, לפי המאוחר.
@ref s.63(b) (src:464)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
      readings IS A `Readings of the dates of section 63`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 63(b) — the day 18 months from the commencement day, under the readings` facts readings MEANS
    `s 63 — the day the Law commences, N months from the day` 18
        (`s 63(a)(1) — the commencement day, under the readings` facts readings)
        `, under the readings` readings

@ref s.63(b) (src:464)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
      readings IS A `Readings of the dates of section 63`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 63(b) — the day Chapter 6 commences, under the readings` facts readings MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `the day regulations under section 46 came into force, if any`
    WHEN JUST d
    THEN `s 63 — the later of`
             (`s 63(b) — the day 18 months from the commencement day, under the readings` facts readings)
             `and` d
    WHEN NOTHING
    THEN `section 63(b) starts Chapter 6 at the later of 18 months from the commencement day and the entry into force of regulations under section 46, and none are in the sources`

@ref s.63(b) (src:464)
@export The day Chapter 6 (financial sanctions) of the Israeli Law on work on refrigeration and air-conditioning systems commences (section 63(b)): the later of 18 months from the commencement day and the entry into force of regulations under section 46; refused if no section 46 regulation is known
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63` @desc The Law's publication day, the day the section 59 regulations came into force, and the day any section 46 regulations came into force (absent if none are known)
GIVETH A DATE
`the day Chapter 6 commences under section 63(b)` facts MEANS
    `s 63(b) — the day Chapter 6 commences, under the readings` facts `the readings of the dates taken`

@ref s.63(b) (src:464)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      facts IS A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
      readings IS A `Readings of the dates of section 63`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63(b) — under the readings, Chapter 6 has commenced on the day` day facts readings MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   day LESS THAN (`s 63(b) — the day 18 months from the commencement day, under the readings` facts readings)
        THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER facts's `the day regulations under section 46 came into force, if any`
            WHEN JUST d  THEN day AT LEAST d
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `section 63(b) starts Chapter 6 at the later of 18 months from the commencement day and the entry into force of regulations under section 46, and none are in the sources`

@ref s.63(b) (src:464)
@export Whether Chapter 6 (financial sanctions) of the Israeli Law on work on refrigeration and air-conditioning systems had commenced on the given day (section 63(b)); refused when the answer depends on section 46 regulations that are not known
GIVEN day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about, for example the day of the act
      facts IS A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63` @desc The Law's publication day, the day the section 59 regulations came into force, and the day any section 46 regulations came into force (absent if none are known)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` day `given the facts` facts MEANS
    `s 63(b) — under the readings, Chapter 6 has commenced on the day` day facts `the readings of the dates taken`

-- The closed-world alternative (fork F-C-8): "no regulation under section 46 is known" is read as "none is in
-- force on the day asked about", so Chapter 6 has not commenced.  The text does not say this; it is the reading
-- under which a missing instrument means "not yet".
@ref s.63(b) (src:464)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      facts IS A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
      readings IS A `Readings of the dates of section 63`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63(b) — reading no regulation under section 46 as none in force, Chapter 6 has commenced on the day` day facts readings MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   day LESS THAN (`s 63(b) — the day 18 months from the commencement day, under the readings` facts readings)
        THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER facts's `the day regulations under section 46 came into force, if any`
            WHEN JUST d  THEN day AT LEAST d
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

§§ `The alternative readings of the dates, as records (forks F-C-1 to F-C-4)`

-- Each alternative is the record of readings below; calling the date functions above with it is the alternative.

@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462); s.63(a)(2) (src:463); s.63(b) (src:464)
GIVEN calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A `Readings of the dates of section 63`
`the readings of the dates with IL s.10(c) applied, for the calendar` calendar MEANS
    `Readings of the dates of section 63` WITH
        `IL s.10(c) is applied to a period counted from another date` IS TRUE
        `the Law commences on the day after a period of months ends` IS FALSE
        `the three months of paragraph (1) run from the later of the two days` IS FALSE
        `the calendar of rest days` IS calendar

@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462); s.63(a)(2) (src:463); s.63(b) (src:464)
GIVETH A `Readings of the dates of section 63`
`the readings of the dates with commencement on the day after a period ends` MEANS
    `Readings of the dates of section 63` WITH
        `IL s.10(c) is applied to a period counted from another date` IS FALSE
        `the Law commences on the day after a period of months ends` IS TRUE
        `the three months of paragraph (1) run from the later of the two days` IS FALSE
        `the calendar of rest days` IS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS EMPTY

@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462); s.63(a)(2) (src:463); s.63(b) (src:464)
GIVETH A `Readings of the dates of section 63`
`the readings of the dates with the three months counted from the later of the two days` MEANS
    `Readings of the dates of section 63` WITH
        `IL s.10(c) is applied to a period counted from another date` IS FALSE
        `the Law commences on the day after a period of months ends` IS FALSE
        `the three months of paragraph (1) run from the later of the two days` IS TRUE
        `the calendar of rest days` IS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS EMPTY

@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462); s.63(a)(2) (src:463)
GIVETH A `Readings of the regime of section 63(a)`
`the readings of the regime with a mixed system governed by the later paragraph` MEANS
    `Readings of the regime of section 63(a)` WITH
        `how a system with several refrigerants is classified` IS `paragraph (1) governs a system only if every one of its refrigerants is as stated in it`
        `how a listed refrigerant whose use is not permitted is classified` IS `such a refrigerant is not as stated in paragraph (1), so paragraph (2) governs`

@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461-462); s.63(a)(2) (src:463)
